Here's a Java code that demonstrates how to use Jsoup library to parse HTML and extract specific information.

```java
import org.jsoup.Jsoup;
import org.jsoup.nodes.Document;
import org.jsoup.select.Elements;

public class HtmlParser {

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String html = "<html><head></head><body>Hello World!</body></html>";
        Document document = parseHtml(html);
        
        // Get all body tags
        Elements bodyTags = document.getElementsByTag("body");
        
        for (Element tag : bodyTags) {
            System.out.println(tag.text());
        }
    }

    public static Document parseHtml(String html) {
        return Jsoup.parse(html);
    }
}
```

This code will print out the text of all `body` tags in the given HTML.

